LOK Calc: a new chart lands beside its data

FuInsertChart positions a chart away from aPositionRange. With request
arguments (a kit client gives the range in FN_PARAM_5) that range was
the cursor cell alone, so the chart went right next to the cursor and
over the data it charts. Position it from the requested data range,
as the dialog path does with the marked cells.

diff --git a/sc/source/ui/drawfunc/fuins2.cxx b/sc/source/ui/drawfunc/fuins2.cxx
index b0169d0..0a4e3dc 100644
--- a/sc/source/ui/drawfunc/fuins2.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/drawfunc/fuins2.cxx
@@ -452,6 +452,14 @@ FuInsertChart::FuInsertChart(ScTabViewShell& rViewSh, vcl::Window* pWin, ScDrawV
             aRangeString = static_cast<const SfxStringItem*>(pItem)->GetValue();
 
         aPositionRange = rViewSh.GetViewData().GetCurPos();
+        // The chart goes beside its data, not over it.
+        if (pRange)
+        {
+            const ScRangeList aData = *sctools::chartRanges(rViewSh.GetViewData().GetDocument(), pRange->GetValue());
+            aPositionRange = aData[0];
+            for (size_t i = 1; i < aData.size(); ++i)
+                aPositionRange.ExtendTo(aData[i]);
+        }
     }
     else
     {
